# EMDR — split changelog (app vs internal)

After every coding turn, **classify the work before you write the bullet.** Do not dump one mixed note. `/changelog` (“What's new”) is for people using the **signed-in app**, not for admin or platform.

Parser: `lib/changelog-public.ts`. Do not rely on the filter to clean a sloppy bullet — label it correctly.

## Classify (pick one)

Ask: **Would someone in `/app` notice this?**

| Goes on `/changelog` (no prefix) | Stays off the public page (`[internal]`) |
|---|---|
| Session, visual sets, voice, intake, composer | `/admin`, platform settings, Coolify, Docker |
| Login, create account, password, passkey, Google | Cursor rules, Mem0, tests, lint, scripts |
| Onboarding, billing, upgrade, trial, account delete | Marketing site (`/`, `/blog`, `/learn`, `/editorial`) |
| Settings, sidebar, threads, memory sets | SEO, robots, sitemap, Meta Pixel, GTM, JSON-LD |
| In-app help, crisis, consent gate | Infra, env, webhooks, secrets, ports |

If the turn mixed both, write **two bullets** (one public, one `[internal]`). Never fuse them.

## How to write the bullet

Append under `[Unreleased]` → Added / Changed / Fixed / Removed. Newest **last** in that subsection.

```md
# ✅ Public — short, what the user sees (no prefix)
- Password show/hide on login
- AI agent-guided sessions can start a set with voice

# ✅ Internal — prefix required
- [internal] Admin Users directory restyle (`app/admin/users/page.tsx`)
- [internal] Cursor rule changelog-split — classify public vs internal bullets

# ❌ BAD — one dump (admin + app + files)
- Auth + Admin SEO + Coolify healthcheck (`AuthShell.tsx`, `/admin/seo`, port **3471**)
```

Public bullets:

- English, sentence case, **one idea**
- No **BLS**, no file paths, no CSS classes, no `lib/…`, no ports
- No “admin”, “platform”, “Coolify”, “ISR”, “GTM”

`[public]` only to **force** a rare user-facing note the filter would hide. Never use it for admin/platform.

